      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "> Would be good to clarify what has changed since you last PR'd this: #31504.\r\n\r\n1. CMake's de-duplication behaviour has stabilised.\r\n\r\n2. There is now a concrete motivation beyond log noise: extending the Guix warnings-as-errors treatment to Darwin (https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/b12a70f330d0ffcc3064ecf2643f8cfe765cf9c8) is blocked on the \"ignoring duplicate libraries\" warnings this PR silences.\r\n\r\nFrom https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/31504#issuecomment-2609542602:\r\n> Also not sure. Seems like this was [introduced in 3.29](https://cmake.org/cmake/help/latest/policy/CMP0156.html), but then the behaviour was changed again 2 versions later [in 3.31](https://cmake.org/cmake/help/latest/policy/CMP0179.html). Would we be opting into that as well? Then, depending on the version, we'd potentially have CMake behaving 3 different ways at link time.\r\n\r\nReworked to avoid the intermediate behaviour of CMake 3.29 or 3.30.",
